---
const genreTags = [
	'Afro House',
	'Tech House',
	'Progressive House',
	'Techno',
	'Dance',
	'Hip-Hop',
	'R&B',
	'Moombahton',
];
---

<section id="about" class="relative bg-ink py-24">
	<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-16 px-6 lg:grid-cols-[0.9fr_1.1fr] lg:items-start">
		<div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28">
			<span class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.3em] text-accent-3 uppercase">About</span>
			<h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-4xl text-white uppercase sm:text-5xl">The Sound of<br /> No Limits</h2>

			<div class="mt-8 aspect-square w-full max-w-sm rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-gradient-to-br from-surface to-ink">
				<div class="flex h-full items-center justify-center">
					<span class="font-display text-6xl text-white/10">DJ MAC</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<!-- TODO: replace the placeholder above with a real DJ MAC press photo -->

			<div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
				{
					genreTags.map((tag) => (
						<span class="rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium tracking-wider text-zinc-300 uppercase">
							{tag}
						</span>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="space-y-8">
			<p class="border-l-2 border-accent pl-6 text-xl leading-relaxed font-medium text-white sm:text-2xl">
				DJ MAC is a genre-bending selector known for fusing the hypnotic pulse of Afro House and Tech
				House with the raw energy of Hip-Hop and R&B. Equal parts curator and crowd-reader, DJ MAC
				builds sets that move fluidly between underground electronic depth and mainstream urban heat —
				never losing the room, never playing it safe.
			</p>

			<div class="space-y-6 text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 sm:text-lg">
				<p>
					DJ MAC's story starts at the intersection of two worlds — the pulsing basslines of
					underground electronic clubs and the head-nodding swagger of Hip-Hop and R&B radio. Rather
					than choosing a lane, DJ MAC built a sound around the space between genres, training an ear
					equally on the rolling grooves of Tech House and the smooth cadence of urban classics. That
					refusal to specialize became the signature: an artist who speaks fluently in Afro House
					polyrhythms and Moombahton bounce alike.
				</p>
				<p>
					At the core of every set is a simple philosophy: tempo is a tool, not a rulebook. A night
					might open with the hypnotic, slow-building tension of Progressive House, pivot into the
					driving four-on-the-floor push of Techno, then detonate into the sharp-edged energy of
					Moombahton — each transition engineered to keep the crowd's momentum climbing, never flat.
					It's DJing as storytelling, where every track earns its place and every shift in tempo has
					a reason behind it.
				</p>
				<p>
					What ties it all together is an obsession with reading the room. DJ MAC treats every gig —
					from an intimate club night to a festival main stage — as a live conversation with the
					crowd, adjusting in real time to keep the energy exactly where it needs to be. The result
					is a set that feels less like a playlist and more like a journey: unpredictable in the best
					way, and built to leave every dancefloor wanting one more track.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
